      "comments": [
        {
          "author": "frivoal",
          "path": "css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-with-floats-008.html",
          "line": 7,
          "commit_id": "2b06abee5ecf3e41fed099279c532e152c0c1555",
          "review_state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/46734#discussion_r1642164764",
          "body": "Based on the `continue: collapse` behavior, this test seems right. But in the `continue: discard` behavior, the float itself would be fragmented as well. It still would not leak out of the IFC, but you would not see all of it.\r\n\r\nHere is one suggestion that would enable you to confirm that floats are contained and do not affect subsequent content, working in both cases:\r\n* add a fixed-height of `4lh` to the container\r\n* don't give a background color to the float inside the container\r\n* add this to the markup after the container\r\n  ```html\r\n  <div class=\"float green\"></div>\r\n  <div class=\"abs\"></div>\r\n  ```\r\n* add this to the style \r\n  ```css\r\n   .abs {\r\n      width: 50px;\r\n      height: 50px;\r\n      margin: 4px;\r\n      background-color: red;\r\n      z-index: -1;\r\n  }\r\n      .green {\r\n      background: green;\r\n  }\r\n  ```\r\nThat way, we cannot see if the float is preseved in place or fragmented, but we can see if it leaks out of the container forcing the green float to the right, and revealing the red abspos, or if it correctly has no effect outside of its BFC.\r\n",
          "fixed_before_merge": true
        },
        {
          "author": "frivoal",
          "path": "css/css-overflow/line-clamp/webkit-line-clamp-044.html",
          "line": 25,
          "commit_id": "2b06abee5ecf3e41fed099279c532e152c0c1555",
          "review_state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/46734#discussion_r1642201051",
          "body": "For the same reason as discussed for floats-008, this test works with `continue: collapse` but not with `continue: discard`. If you add  to the float, then I think it does work.\r\n```suggestion\r\n    break-inside: avoid;`\r\n  }\r\n```",
          "fixed_before_merge": true
        },
